title: "大模型的小练习（二）：三行朗顿蚂蚁的精确逃逸时间"
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24540968"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
authors:
  - name: "yutitan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yutitan/langton-ant-three-rows"
url: "https://github.com/yutitan/langton-ant-three-rows"
abstract: >-
  Exact escape time of Langton's ant on three-row boards: S(1)=2, S(2)=12 and,
  for every n>=3, S(n)=10n-12 (n even) and S(n)=10n-13 (n odd). The lower
  bound is due to Etse (MFCS 2026); this record supplies the all-width
  upper-bound proof, a computer-assisted argument based on a finite
  34-record certificate and an induction replacing a four-column end block by
  a two-column block (S(n) <= S(n-2)+20 for n>=8). All claims are checked by
  independent programs included in the repository.
keywords:
  - Langton's ant
  - cellular automata
  - escaping time
  - computer-assisted proof
  - AI-assisted exploration
license: MIT
notes: >-
  Series: 大模型的小练习（二） (LLM Exercises II); the first entry is
  https://github.com/yutitan/wowii-conjecture-138. Derived with GPT 6.2 Astra
  (OpenAI Codex, model gpt-6.2-astra) on 2026-11-25 17:55:34 UTC and
  independently verified with DeepSeek Harness. This is a public record of a
  personal AI-assisted exploration and makes no priority claim. The lower
  bound is due to K. R. Etse, "How Long Can The Escaping Ant Be Confined?",
  MFCS 2026, DOI 10.4230/LIPIcs.MFCS.2026.49; the four-row analogue was solved
  by H. Ke, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23675964.
  Archived at Zenodo under DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24540968 (concept DOI
  10.5281/zenodo.24540967; release v1.0.0).
